      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000122290,
      "SummaryText": "The accidental release prevention and emergency response policies for the facility: This facility complies with NFPA-58 requirements for LP-Gas storage, and it is our policy to adhere to all applicable federal, state, and local laws. If an emergency were to occur, it is our policy to notify the Town of Patterson Fire Department and request that they respond to the emergency.\nRegulated Substances handled at the facility. This facility is a bulk terminal storing LPG for sale and transportation to residential, commercial, and industrial clients. The facility consists of four 30,000-gallon tanks.\nThe worst-case and alternative release scenarios. The worst-case scenario is failure of one 30,000-gallon storage tank when filled to the greatest amount allowed (88% at 60F), resulting in a vapor cloud explosion. The resulting distance to the endpoint extends offsite, and public receptors are within the distance to the endpoint.\nOur alternative release scenario is a break in a 0.5-inch diameter pipe, leading to a 10-minute release and explosion. The resulting distance to the endpoint extends offsite, and public receptors are within the distance to the endpoint.\nThe general accidental release prevention program and chemical-specific prevention steps. This facility falls under the jurisdiction of the  EPA\u0092s accident prevention rule, the OSHA PSM standard, and all applicable state and local codes and regulations. The propane system was designed, installed, and will be maintained in accordance with NFPA-58 and state law.\nFive-year accident history. The facility has not had an accident involving propane that caused deaths, injuries, property or environmental damage, evacuations, or sheltering in place.\nThe emergency response program. In the event of an emergency involving our propane system, it is our policy to notify the Town of Patterson Fire Department and request that they help respond to the emergency. We have coordinated our response plans with the fire department; members of"
    },
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 1,
      "FacilityID": 1000122290,
      "SummaryText": "the fire department have inspected our propane system and conducted a joint exercise with us.\nPlanned changes to improve safety. None."
    }
  ]
